<title>ESTONIA: UP TO 20 MLN KROONS FROZEN IN ACCOUNTS - REPORT.</title>
<headline>UP TO 20 MLN KROONS FROZEN IN ACCOUNTS - REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 15 to 20 million kroons in funds held by Estonian banks has been frozen in two St Petersburg banks by the Russian tax police, newspaper Aripaev said on Friday, citing central bank and bank figures.</p>
<p>The accounts of several Estonian, Latvian and one Lithuanian banks were frozen with a total of 40 million kroons blocked, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>It quoted a press spokesperson of the St Petersburg tax police as saying that the police were seeking tax payments of 400 million kroons from the banks.</p>
<p>Ivar lukk of Forekspank, one of the banks affected by the action, was quoted by the newspaper as saying that the action of the tax police was unfounded and that the bank had already initiated legal action.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9201/2 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
